Subject: Register VM: interpreter activations of functions the unit holds a body for, counted per function (statistics build)

What this does
  - quickjs.c: with QJS_AOT_ICOUNT defined and QJS_AOT_STATS set in the environment, `js_aot_icount[]` (one counter per unit table index, allocated at the first bind) is incremented where the interpreter starts a function whose unit binding was dropped by the profitability gate, or whose compiled entry handed the whole call back (JS_CALL_FLAG_AOT_DEOPT): js_regvm_execute, regvm_t_call_record, regvm_t_call_method_record, regvm_t_construct_record and regvm_light_prepare. `qjs_aot_icount_table()` exports the table; the generated unit's statistics report (`aot interp fn=...`) reads it through a weak reference.
  - Without QJS_AOT_ICOUNT, AOT_ICOUNT() is an empty statement: no code in any call path.

Why we need it
  The share of calls that run in the interpreter, per function, is what the generator's coverage work is measured by (a function the unit holds a body for that runs in the register interpreter is a coverage defect). The sampling profile gives the share by handler, not by function.

Soundness
  Read-only counters; nothing a compiled body or the interpreter reads.

Failure modes
  A generator resumed in the interpreter counts once per resume. A bytecode without its own table slot (a twin of the bound one) is not counted.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -2192,6 +2192,19 @@
 static void aot_run_free(JSRuntime *rt);
 extern uint64_t js_aot_bound_count;
 extern uint64_t js_aot_enter_count;
+#if defined(QJS_AOT_ICOUNT) && QJS_AOT
+/* Interpreter activations of functions the unit holds a body for (QJS_AOT_STATS=1 builds that define QJS_AOT_ICOUNT): one counter per
+   unit table index, allocated at the first bind. An activation is counted where the interpreter starts a function whose binding was
+   dropped (gated) or whose compiled entry handed the whole call back. */
+extern uint64_t *js_aot_icount;
+#define AOT_ICOUNT(b_, fl_) \
+    do { if (unlikely(js_aot_icount != NULL) && (b_)->aot_index != UINT32_MAX && \
+                      ((b_)->aot_fn == NULL || ((fl_) & JS_CALL_FLAG_AOT_DEOPT))) \
+             js_aot_icount[(b_)->aot_index]++; } while (0)
+#endif
+#endif
+#ifndef AOT_ICOUNT
+#define AOT_ICOUNT(b_, fl_) ((void)0)
 #endif
 
 /* Shared backing for lazily deserialized function bodies.
